OL,3,GNEWSARunner walks final London Marathon
OL,4,Amile six months on
OL,5,
OL,6,FA runner who suffered a cardiac arrest
OL,7,Fat the 25th mile of the London Marathon
OL,8,Fhas finally "finished what I started" -
OL,9,Fby walking the last mile, six months
OL,10,Flater.
OL,12,FGareth Hopkins, 43, a paramedic from
OL,13,FHoddesdon, Hertfordshire, collapsed
OL,14,Fduring the race on 26 April when his
OL,15,Fheart stopped due to severe
OL,16,Frhabdomyolysis, caused by overheating.
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
